Feature: artie generate's options: reason steps kept, text made inputs
  spec/PLAN-SCRIPT-GENERATOR.md, rules 4 and 4a. By default a value the
  reasoner chose is frozen as the constant it was. With --keep-reason, a step
  where the reasoner chose a value stays an act(intent = ...) step, for a choice that
  should depend on the state at run time; the script then needs a reasoner.
  With --inputs, literal text the run sent under a field's name becomes an
  input of that name, the run's text its default.

  Background:
    Given the file "run.trace.yaml" is
      """
      ---
      run:
        inputs:
          owner:
            value: acme
            given: given
      ---
      mode: script
      say: enter {entry}
      line: 1
      params:
        entry: http://localhost:8392/
      opens: true
      outcome: done
      ---
      mode: intent
      say: open the repository acme
      line: 2
      within: 1
      params:
        relation: repos-get
        owner: acme
      values:
        owner:
          value: acme
          from:
            - input: owner
      reason:
        template: open the repository $owner
        slots:
          owner:
            value: acme
            from:
              - input: owner
      opens: true
      outcome: done
      ---
      mode: intent
      say: open an issue titled "Crash on start", saying it was opened by a script
      line: 3
      within: 2
      params:
        relation: open-issue
        title: Crash on start
        body: Opened by a script.
      values:
        title:
          value: Crash on start
          from:
            - words
        body:
          value: Opened by a script.
          from:
            - paraphrase
      reason:
        template: open an issue titled "Crash on start", saying it was opened by a script
        slots: {}
      opens: true
      outcome: new resource
      ---
      mode: intent
      say: 'comment on it: Thanks.'
      line: 4
      within: 3
      params:
        relation: comment
        body: Thanks.
      values:
        body:
          value: Thanks.
          from:
            - words
      reason:
        template: 'comment on it: Thanks.'
        slots: {}
      opens: true
      outcome: new resource
      ---
      mode: intent
      say: close it, since it's done
      line: 5
      within: 3
      params:
        relation: close
        reason: completed
      values:
        reason:
          value: completed
          from:
            - chosen
      reason:
        template: close it, since it's done
        slots: {}
      outcome: done
      """

  Scenario: --keep-reason keeps a step whose value the reasoner chose, and the script says it needs a reasoner
    When artie is run with
      | argument       |
      | generate       |
      | run.trace.yaml |
      | --out          |
      | gen.kts        |
      | --keep-reason  |
    Then artie exits 0
    And artie prints
      | line                                                |
      | wrote gen.kts: 0 values to review, 1 reason step kept |
      | wrote gen.pins.yaml: 0 forms and 0 links pinned     |
      | wrote gen.derivation.yaml: 6 derivations            |
    And the file "gen.kts" reads
      ```kotlin
      // Generated by artie generate from run.trace.yaml.
      // Every selection as that run made it, nested as it nested; where the reasoner chose a value, its reason step is kept.
      // What it was offered is pinned in gen.pins.yaml, held to before every act.
      // 1 step calls the model on every run: artie run needs --reasoner.
      //   artie run gen.kts owner=acme --reasoner claude
      val owner by input()

      heart("http://localhost:8392/") {
          act("repos-get", "owner" to owner, intent = "open the repository $owner") {
              act("open-issue", intent = """open an issue titled "Crash on start", saying it was opened by a script""", fields = {
                  "title" to "Crash on start"
                  "body" to "Opened by a script."
              }) {
                  sync()
                  act("comment", "body" to "Thanks.", intent = "comment on it: Thanks.") {}
                  act(intent = "close it, since it's done")
              }
          }
      }
      ```

  Scenario: --inputs makes the text the run sent under a field's name an input, the run's text its default
    When artie is run with
      | argument       |
      | generate       |
      | run.trace.yaml |
      | --out          |
      | gen.kts        |
      | --inputs       |
      | title          |
    Then artie exits 0
    And the file "gen.kts" reads
      ```kotlin
      // Generated by artie generate from run.trace.yaml.
      // Every selection as that run made it, nested as it nested, with no model.
      // What it was offered is pinned in gen.pins.yaml, held to before every act.
      // A line marked "review:" holds a value the reasoner chose: check it before keeping the script.
      //   artie run gen.kts owner=acme
      val owner by input()
      val title by input(default = "Crash on start")

      heart("http://localhost:8392/") {
          act("repos-get", "owner" to owner, intent = "open the repository $owner") {
              act("open-issue", intent = """open an issue titled "Crash on start", saying it was opened by a script""", fields = {
                  "title" to title
                  "body" to "Opened by a script."
              }) {
                  sync()
                  act("comment", "body" to "Thanks.", intent = "comment on it: Thanks.") {}
                  act("close", intent = "close it, since it's done", fields = {
                      "reason" to "completed" // review: the reasoner chose it, asked "close it, since it's done"
                  })
              }
          }
      }
      ```

  Scenario Outline: A field --inputs names must have been sent once, with one value, under a name no input has
    When artie is run with
      | argument       |
      | generate       |
      | run.trace.yaml |
      | --out          |
      | gen.kts        |
      | --inputs       |
      | <inputs>       |
    Then artie exits 2
    And artie's last line is: <last>

    Examples:
      | inputs  | last                                        |
      | body    | --inputs body: the run sent more than one body |
      | subject | --inputs subject: the run sent no subject   |
      | owner   | --inputs owner: owner is an input already   |
